# PART B: GITHUB SOURCE CODE UPLOAD

## STEP 14: CREATE GITHUB ACCOUNT

1. Open https://github.com/
2. Click Sign Up.
3. Enter email address.
4. Create username and password.
5. Complete registration.
6. Log in.

## STEP 15: CREATE GITHUB REPOSITORY

1. Click the + icon.
2. Select New Repository.
3. Enter repository name: `program-6`.
4. Select Public or Private.
5. Leave Add README unchecked.
6. Click Create Repository.
7. Copy the HTTPS repository URL.

Repository URL format:

```text
https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/program-6.git
```

## STEP 16: CONFIGURE GIT IDENTITY

Open Ubuntu Terminal inside P06.

Set username:

```bash
git config --global user.name "YOUR_NAME"
```

Set email:

```bash
git config --global user.email "YOUR_EMAIL"
```

Verify:

```bash
git config --global --list
```

## STEP 17: INITIALIZE GIT

Execute:

```bash
git init
```

## STEP 18: CONNECT PROJECT TO GITHUB

Execute:

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/program-6.git
```

Verify:

```bash
git remote -v
```

If origin already exists:

```bash
git remote set-url origin https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/program-6.git
```

## STEP 19: PUSH SOURCE CODE TO GITHUB

Add project files:

```bash
git add .
```

Commit:

```bash
git commit -m "Initial commit"
```

Rename branch:

```bash
git branch -M main
```

Push:

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

Complete GitHub authentication if requested.

Expected output:

```text
main -> main
branch 'main' set up to track 'origin/main'
```

Verify the source files in your GitHub repository.

**GitHub source code upload completed.**

---

# PART C: GITHUB CONTAINER REGISTRY (GHCR)

## STEP 20: CREATE GITHUB PERSONAL ACCESS TOKEN

1. Open https://github.com/settings/tokens
2. Select Personal Access Tokens.
3. Select Tokens (classic).
4. Click Generate new token.
5. Select Generate new token (classic).
6. Enter token name: `GHCR-Program6`.
7. Select expiration.
8. Enable the following permissions:

```text
read:packages
write:packages
```

9. Click Generate token.
10. Copy and securely save the token.

IMPORTANT: Never share your token or upload it to GitHub.

## STEP 21: TAG DOCKER IMAGE FOR GHCR

Open Ubuntu Terminal inside P06.

Execute:

```bash
docker tag program-6 ghcr.io/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/program-6:latest
```

Replace `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME` with your GitHub username.

## STEP 22: LOGIN TO GHCR

Execute:

```bash
echo "YOUR_GITHUB_PAT" | docker login ghcr.io -u YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME --password-stdin
```

Replace:

- YOUR_GITHUB_PAT with your actual GitHub Personal Access Token.
- YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME with your GitHub username.

Expected output:

```text
Login Succeeded
```

## STEP 23: PUSH DOCKER IMAGE TO GHCR

Execute:

```bash
docker push ghcr.io/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/program-6:latest
```

Wait until all image layers are uploaded.

Expected output:

```text
latest: digest: sha256:...
```

## STEP 24: VERIFY GITHUB PACKAGES

1. Open GitHub.
2. Click your profile picture.
3. Select Your profile.
4. Open Packages.
5. Find the program-6 container package.
6. Open it.
7. Verify the latest image tag.

**GitHub Container Registry upload completed.**

